@* Renders its content only when the signed-in user holds the given
   permission code (or the Administrator wildcard). Wrap an action control —
   a create / edit / delete button — so it disappears for users who lack the
   permission. The API still enforces the same permission, so this is a UX
   layer (don't show what you can't do), not the security boundary.

   The policy decision itself lives in SimfActionGate, in the shared
   component library, because SimfDataGrid has to gate the buttons it renders
   itself and cannot reach a Control Panel component. This stays as the name CP
   page markup uses, so no page changed; there is one implementation underneath. *@
<SimfActionGate Permission="@Permission">@ChildContent</SimfActionGate>
